I have everything needed. Here is my report on the Owner creation flow.

## Summary

Key finding on `sharesHousehold`: it does NOT currently exist anywhere in the production code (not in the `Owner` entity, not in the generated `OwnerDto`, and not in `openapi.yml`). It appears only in an acceptance test, `Cp17Tests.java`, which expects the created-owner response JSON to contain a `sharesHousehold` boolean. This is clearly a feature that still needs to be implemented across the OpenAPI schema, the entity/mapper, and the create-owner controller logic.

---

### 1. Owner REST controller — POST/create method

File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain9/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

The class implements the generated `OwnersApi` interface. The create handler is `addOwner` (lines 125-162), mapped to `POST /api/owners`:

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    owner.setTelephone(normalizeTelephone(owner.getTelephone()));
    if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
    }
    if (isDailyRegistrationLimitReached()) {
        throw new DailyOwnerRegistrationLimitException(
            "The maximum of " + MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY
                + " owners that may be registered today has already been reached");
    }
    if (isDuplicateTelephone(owner)) {
        throw new DuplicateOwnerException("An owner with telephone "
            + owner.getTelephone() + " already exists");
    }
    if (isDuplicateEmail(owner)) {
        throw new DuplicateOwnerException("An owner with email "
            + owner.getEmail() + " already exists");
    }
    if (isCityOwnerLimitReached(owner.getCity())) {
        throw new CityOwnerLimitException("The city " + owner.getCity()
            + " already contains the maximum of " + MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY + " owners");
    }
    int membershipNumber = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().size() + 1;
    owner.setMembershipNumber(membershipNumber);
    owner.setMembershipTier(membershipNumber <= FOUNDING_MEMBERSHIP_LIMIT ? "FOUNDING" : "STANDARD");
    owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getLastName()));
    owner.setCity(resolveCity(owner.getCity()));
    owner.setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(owner.getCity()));
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

Notable: this controller already derives several computed/transient fields at creation (`membershipNumber`, `membershipTier`, `namesakeCount`, `customerCode`, `resolveCity`). A `sharesHousehold` flag would naturally be computed here too. The class has helpers that iterate `clinicService.findAllOwners()` and compare fields case-insensitively — the same pattern needed for "another owner already has the same address and city." There is also a `resolveCity(...)` (title-casing) and `nextCustomerCode(...)` that transform the city before save, which matters for any address+city comparison ordering.

There is also a v2 controller (list-with-pagination only, no create): `/home/daniel/.../rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java`.

---

### 2. Owner entity/model

File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain9/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

`@Entity @Table(name = "owners")`, extends `Person` (which supplies `firstName`/`lastName`). Fields:
- `address` (`@Column(name="address") @NotEmpty String`) — line 39-41
- `city` (`@Column(name="city") @NotEmpty String`) — line 43-45
- `telephone` (`@NotEmpty @Digits(...) @Pattern("^[0-9]{10}$")`) — line 47-51
- `email` (String) — line 53-54
- `registrationDate` (LocalDate) — line 56-57
- `membershipNumber` (Integer, `membership_number`)
- `customerCode` (String, `customer_code`)
- `membershipTier` (String, `membership_tier`)
- `namesakeCount` (Integer, `@Transient` — computed, not persisted) — line 72-73
- `pets` (`Set<Pet>`, OneToMany)

Note the pattern for the transient `namesakeCount` is the likely model for adding a transient `sharesHousehold` boolean.

---

### 3. Owner DTO / response class

Generated file: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain9/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerDto.java`

Yes, it is generated from OpenAPI (`@Generated(value = "org.openapitools.codegen.languages.SpringCodegen" ...)`, generator 7.23.0) via `openapi.yml`. It is NOT checked into `src/`; it only exists under `target/generated-sources`.

It does NOT have a `sharesHousehold` field. Its fields: `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone, email, registrationDate, id, displayName, initials, membershipNumber, customerCode, membershipTier (enum FOUNDING/STANDARD), namesakeCount, pets`.

Because the DTO is generated, adding `sharesHousehold` requires editing `openapi.yml` (the `Owner` schema), not the generated file directly. Related generated DTOs: `OwnerFieldsDto.java` (request body — editable input fields) and `OwnerPageDto.java`, in the same directory.

---

### 4. Mapper (Owner entity <-> DTO)

File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain9/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`

MapStruct interface (`@Mapper(uses = PetMapper.class)`). It maps `Owner` -> `OwnerDto` and uses `@Mapping(... expression="java(...)")` for computed fields `displayName` and `initials`, with `default` methods implementing them. Key parts:

```java
@Mapper(uses = PetMapper.class)
public interface OwnerMapper {

    @Mapping(target = "displayName", expression = "java(toDisplayName(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "initials", expression = "java(toInitials(owner))")
    OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);

    default String toDisplayName(Owner owner) { ... "LastName, FirstName" ... }
    default String toInitials(Owner owner) { ... "J.S." ... }

    Owner toOwner(OwnerDto ownerDto);

    @Mapping(target = "id", ignore = true)
    @Mapping(target = "pets", ignore = true)
    Owner toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerDto);

    List<OwnerDto> toOwnerDtoCollection(Collection<Owner> ownerCollection);
    Collection<Owner> toOwners(Collection<OwnerDto> ownerDtos);

    default OwnerPageDto toOwnerPageDto(@NonNull Page<Owner> ownerPage) { ... }
}
```

Since fields on `Owner` and `OwnerDto` are auto-mapped by name, a `sharesHousehold` on both would flow through automatically; if it's computed rather than stored, it can be done here via an `@Mapping(... expression=...)` like `displayName`, or set on the entity in the controller (as `namesakeCount` is). MapStruct impl is generated into `target/generated-sources/annotations/.../OwnerMapperImpl.java`.

---

### 5. Repository / service query methods

Service interface: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain9/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` (impl: `ClinicServiceImpl.java` in same package). Owner-related methods (lines 56-61):
- `Owner findOwnerById(int id)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAllOwners()`
- `Page<Owner> findOwners(String lastName, Pageable pageable)`
- `void saveOwner(Owner owner)`
- `void deleteOwner(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findOwnerByLastName(String lastName)`

Repository interface: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain9/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)` (starts-with) and paged overload
- `Owner findById(int id)`
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()` and `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

Implementations: `repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`. There is no existing "find by address/city" query — the controller does the household check in-memory via `findAllOwners()`.

---

### 6. OpenAPI spec

File: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain9/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`

- Create-owner endpoint: `POST /owners`, `operationId: addOwner`, request body `$ref '#/components/schemas/OwnerFields'`, `201` response `$ref '#/components/schemas/Owner'` (path block starts at line 65).
- Schemas (line numbers): `OwnerFields` at 1991 (input: firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone, email, registrationDate; required firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone), `Owner` at 2054 (allOf OwnerFields + id, displayName, initials, membershipNumber, customerCode, membershipTier, namesakeCount, pets — all readOnly except pets which is required), `OwnerPage` at 2121.
- There is NO `sharesHousehold` property in the `Owner` schema. To surface it in the generated `OwnerDto`, a new read-only boolean property must be added to the `Owner` schema here (around lines 2104-2118, alongside `namesakeCount`).

---

### 7. Existing tests for owner creation

Controller test: `/home/daniel/spring-petclinic-rest-long-degradation-test/work/202608011310/spring-just-solve-chain9/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`

